article en "Group identity without transport"
body
  cons paragraph
    cons "FoundationGroupCommitmentCodec is an optional capability separate from the archive codec."
    cons " It returns a complete group commitment and ordered existing v2 entry commitments after depth-aware native and codec-registry validation."
    cons " It produces no GroupArchive transport and has no default-success implementation."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons text "The complete group digest uses domain "
      cons code "NEPL3.Foreign.Group.v2\\0"
      cons text " over exactly a three-element NDF List:"
      nil
    nil
  cons list ordered 1
    cons item none body cons paragraph
      cons "The checked ForeignClosureGroup skeleton, with typed local source lists replaced by empty lists, retaining all other fields and table order."
      nil nil
    cons item none body cons paragraph
      cons "A provenance-indexed List of membership-list sequences."
      nil nil
    cons item none body cons paragraph
      cons "An entry-indexed List of child-first syntax membership-list sequences."
      nil nil
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Every membership list contains the ordered SourceContent v2 commitments defined by the compact entry contract."
    cons " Empty sets and component boundaries are preserved."
    cons " Source commitments include the full Foundation SchemaRef, SourceRef, URI and text."
    cons " Unused local declarations remain included."
    cons " Native-invalid unreferenced provenance or environment rows are not admitted."
    cons " Complete group identity intentionally binds table order and owner/provenance references; per-entry v2 identities retain their existing valid-remapping invariance."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "The operation preserves native occurrence depths/current outer depth, independent codec registry validation, replaced-source-field descriptor checks, skeleton structural validation, individual SourceContent checks and one cumulative admission ledger."
    cons " Missing local declarations and conflicting snapshots reject."
    cons " It charges actual Work, allocations, retained commitments and digest output."
    cons " It does not charge or allocate nonexistent serialized skeleton/GroupArchive buffers."
    cons " Existing archive APIs, transport bytes, identity domains and resource charges remain unchanged."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Returned digests are data, not native validation proofs."
    cons " A consuming Doc/PageSet profile must bind its remaining fields separately and explicitly select new identity domains."
    cons " This capability alone establishes no rendering or historical-corpus success."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons sentence
      cons text "Identity-only document consumption is specified in "
      cons link relative "33-doc-commitment-profile.md" none text "Doc commitment profile"
      cons text "."
      nil
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Identity-only capture does not build the archive union or SourceRef membership storage."
    cons " It orders each local declaration set once, explicitly admits each source, and retains the same exact SourceSnapshot/digest cache and ordered commitment memberships."
    cons " Archive capture keeps its existing union/membership behavior."
    cons " Removing unused transport bookkeeping does not alter either identity preimage or skip source equality, descriptor, native validation or admission checks."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "Identity-only source digest lookup may use a next-index hint local to one canonically ordered source list."
    cons " Every hit still compares the full identity and checks exact snapshot equality."
    cons " Gaps fall back to bounded binary search; the hint is reset for each local list."
    cons " Admission, duplicate rejection, miss-path schema validation and digest framing remain mandatory."
    cons " Archive lookup is unchanged."
    nil
  cons paragraph
    cons "On pointer-atomic targets, identity-only capture may retain one owned local source sequence and its canonical index permutation."
    cons " Exact immutable-storage prefix matches permit sorting only newly appended declarations and merging the two orders."
    cons " The merge rejects equal SourceId/revision across the boundary, regardless of digest."
    cons " Shrinking or unrelated sequences use the ordinary complete ordering path."
    cons " Independent snapshots never require a text comparison merely to reuse an order."
    cons " Returned references always point to the current local input; every source still undergoes admission and exact digest-cache validation."
    cons " Retained snapshots, indices, comparisons and output references are budgeted, and failed preparation leaves prior ordering metadata intact."
    cons " Other targets keep ordinary ordering."
    nil
  nil
